A2. -d1 d2 Gamma - u1 = 0 ; d1^2 Gamma - u2 = 0 ; trace of Hessian away from 0 = 0
    angular mean of symbol of R1^2 = -1/2 ; of R1 R2 = 0 (the p.v. kernels have zero angular mean, so these are the contact coefficients)
A3. |u|^2 (2 pi |z|^2)^2 = 1 ; Du^T Du (pi |z|^3)^2 = [[1, 0], [0, 1]]
A4. second-order identity: True
A5. u is even: True ; coefficient (1/2)(1/2) = 1/4 by construction; oddness of u(x-y) - u(x+y) in x: True
A6. far x-integral minus claim at sample a in (0,2): [0, 0, 0]
